Package: dmlrs
Type: Package
Title: Fast Double / Debiased Machine Learning Implemented in Rust
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Asad", "Gudzevic", email = "asadgudzevic94@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Double / debiased machine learning (Chernozhukov et al., 2018,
    <doi:10.1111/ectj.12097>) for causal inference: partially linear,
    interactive, instrumental variable and difference-in-differences models
    with cross-fitted nuisance functions, multiplier bootstrap and sensitivity
    analysis for omitted confounding. Estimation, including the nuisance
    learners (lasso, logistic regression, random forests, gradient boosting),
    runs in Rust through the 'dml-core' crate, in parallel. Results match the
    Python package 'dml-rs', which is validated against 'DoubleML'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://asadgudzevic94.github.io/dml-rs/, https://github.com/AsadGudzevic94/dml-rs
BugReports: https://github.com/AsadGudzevic94/dml-rs/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: stats
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.80
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
